More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (471–480)
471. Improper Validation of JSON Inputs
JSON Input Validation Vulnerability
Applications fail to validate JSON payloads correctly, allowing attackers to manipulate backend processing.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
472. Insecure Deserialization in APIs
Insecure Deserialization
Applications deserialize untrusted data, potentially leading to code execution or privilege escalation.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $10,000
473. Improper Authorization in GraphQL APIs
GraphQL Authorization Bypass
GraphQL endpoints allow attackers to query unauthorized data.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
474. Excessive Data Exposure in API Responses
API Data Overexposure
APIs return more information than necessary, exposing internal data structures.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
475. Improper Cross-Origin Resource Sharing Configuration
CORS Misconfiguration
Incorrect CORS settings allow malicious websites to access sensitive API responses.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
476. Insecure Webhook Secret Management
Webhook Secret Exposure
Webhook secrets are leaked or poorly protected.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
477. Improper Validation of User-Uploaded Archives
Zip Slip Vulnerability
Attackers upload malicious archives that overwrite server files.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
478. Improper Enforcement of Account Lockout
Account Lockout Bypass
Systems fail to lock accounts after repeated login attempts.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
479. Insecure Handling of HTTP Content-Type Header
Content-Type Header Manipulation
Applications trust the content type provided by the client, allowing malicious payloads.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
480. Improper Validation of OAuth Scopes
OAuth Scope Escalation
Attackers manipulate OAuth scopes to gain higher privileges.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
